From 0c76b44ffbd4e4bad3680582492fc8e37f7e886e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stephen Cheng <stephen.cheng@citrix.com>
Date: Tue, 21 Jul 2026 11:03:46 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] CP-309209: Remove 200000baseLR4_ER4_FR4 link mode (XS8 only)

This patch is for XenServer 8 (XS8) ONLY.

The XS8 kernel (4.19) defines ETHTOOL_LINK_MODE_200000baseSR4_Full_BIT,
200000baseDR4 and 200000baseKR4, but does not define
ETHTOOL_LINK_MODE_200000baseLR4_ER4_FR4_Full_BIT, so the build fails:

  enic_ethtool.c: In function 'enic_get_supp_adv_media_type':
  error: 'ETHTOOL_LINK_MODE_200000baseLR4_ER4_FR4_Full_BIT' undeclared

That 200G link mode cannot exist on the 4.19 kernel anyway, so simply
drop the two ethtool_link_ksettings_add_link_mode() calls that advertise
it. The SR4/DR4 200G modes that the XS8 kernel does provide are kept.

NOTE: This is an XS8-only workaround. Do NOT carry this patch to XS9 or
any newer kernel that defines
ETHTOOL_LINK_MODE_200000baseLR4_ER4_FR4_Full_BIT, as it would drop a
valid 200G media advertisement there.

Signed-off-by: Stephen Cheng <stephen.cheng@citrix.com>
---
 enic_ethtool.c | 5 -----
 1 file changed, 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/enic_ethtool.c b/enic_ethtool.c
index 36e581e..a27be30 100644
--- a/enic_ethtool.c
+++ b/enic_ethtool.c
@@ -515,11 +515,6 @@ enic_get_supp_adv_media_type(struct net_device *netdev,
 			200000baseDR4_Full);
 		ethtool_link_ksettings_add_link_mode(ecmd, advertising,
 			200000baseDR4_Full);
-
-		ethtool_link_ksettings_add_link_mode(ecmd, supported,
-			200000baseLR4_ER4_FR4_Full);
-		ethtool_link_ksettings_add_link_mode(ecmd, advertising,
-			200000baseLR4_ER4_FR4_Full);
 #endif
 		ethtool_link_ksettings_add_link_mode(ecmd, supported, FIBRE);
 		ethtool_link_ksettings_add_link_mode(ecmd, advertising, FIBRE);
-- 
